    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19580" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βασσάρ-α</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰρ], ἡ,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλώπηξ</span>
			, <i>fox,</i> Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				771
			</span></i> (Cyren. acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>dress of Thracian bacchanals,</i> made of <i>fox</i>-skins, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AB</u>
				222
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>Thracian bacchanal,</i> in pl., title of play by <i><span class="en">
				A.
			</span></i>, Sch. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				142
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Callix.
				2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>impudent woman, courtesan,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				771
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1393
			</span></i>.</div>
